{"base_rate":0.3719512195121951,"brier":0.19181737804878046,"bss":0.1788763011300335,"bss_hi":0.31876850325544337,"bss_lo":0.05195383349325195,"chart":{"base":[544.3,68.0],"fp":[180.2,248.4],"lead":"62,232.5 272,208.4 482,193.2 692,178.9","note":{"base":"skill 0.18 — higher than 25% of cities","fp":"low end -2pp, high end +28pp","lead":"day-1 error 1.3 °C — better than 29% of cities","rel":"promised 1% → rained 2%; promised 96% → rained 70%"},"rel":"66,456 190.1,420.5 462.6,327.5 666,162.1"},"country":"VN","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.18850609756097564,"ess":308.7641701740731,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Haiphong</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Haiphong rain forecast is only marginally better than quoting the long-run average, though 5 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (99%), believe about\n<b>76%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(1%), there is still roughly a <b>2%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 656 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-03-26. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nthe station, 8.9 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.18, ranked 159 of\n213 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(94&ndash;180) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>1%</td><td class='num'><b>2%</b></td><td class='num'>129</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>11%</td><td class='num'><b>3%</b></td><td class='num'>61</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>28%</td><td class='num'><b>17%</b></td><td class='num'>72</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>54%</td><td class='num'><b>23%</b></td><td class='num'>64</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>73%</td><td class='num'><b>40%</b></td><td class='num'>67</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>86%</td><td class='num'><b>49%</b></td><td class='num'>59</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>99%</td><td class='num'><b>76%</b></td><td class='num'>204</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">5 of 7 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Haiphong</b> <span class=\"muted\">Vietnam</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag bad\">Barely beats the average</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">5 points off by more than chance</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>0.18</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>94&ndash;180\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 213</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>656 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Haiphong &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Haiphong\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"60.25023255813954,373.5348837209302 96.8239344262295,310.39344262295083 158.10333333333335,240.31805555555624 248.71750000000003,143.125 315.9444776119403,77.76119402985074 363.04,36.50847457627117 407.2973529411765,18.0 407.2973529411765,28.70588235294116 363.04,104.37288135593224 315.9444776119403,153.82089552238804 248.71750000000003,228.4375 158.10333333333335,316.27777777777777 96.8239344262295,370.0655737704918 60.25023255813954,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"246.609756097561\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"246.609756097561\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"60.25023255813954,373.5348837209302 96.8239344262295,370.0655737704918 158.10333333333335,321.3333333333333 248.71750000000003,296.6875 315.9444776119403,235.3134328358209 363.04,203.08474576271186 407.2973529411765,103.64705882352945\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 1%&amp;#10;It rained 2% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 129 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"60.25023255813954\" cy=\"373.5348837209302\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 11%&amp;#10;It rained 3% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 61 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"96.8239344262295\" cy=\"370.0655737704918\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 28%&amp;#10;It rained 17% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 72 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"158.10333333333335\" cy=\"321.3333333333333\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 54%&amp;#10;It rained 23% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 64 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"248.71750000000003\" cy=\"296.6875\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 73%&amp;#10;It rained 40% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 67 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"315.9444776119403\" cy=\"235.3134328358209\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 86%&amp;#10;It rained 49% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 59 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"363.04\" cy=\"203.08474576271186\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 99%&amp;#10;It rained 76% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 204 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"407.2973529411765\" cy=\"103.64705882352945\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(37%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Haiphong the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>autumn</b> (0.42) and least in\n<b>spring</b> (-0.22).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>142</td><td class='num'>32%</td><td class='num'>-0.216</td><td class='num'>26.4%</td></tr><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>177</td><td class='num'>57%</td><td class='num'>0.023</td><td class='num'>24.1%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>162</td><td class='num'>21%</td><td class='num'>0.176</td><td class='num'>8.5%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>175</td><td class='num'>36%</td><td class='num'>0.417</td><td class='num'>14.6%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":20.86481,"lon":106.68345,"n":656,"n_cities":213,"name":"Haiphong","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.06,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.006356589147286822,"n":129,"obs":0.023255813953488372,"sig":false},{"hi":0.2,"lo":0.06,"mean":0.10967213114754099,"n":61,"obs":0.03278688524590164,"sig":false},{"hi":0.43,"lo":0.2,"mean":0.2827777777777778,"n":72,"obs":0.16666666666666666,"sig":true},{"hi":0.65,"lo":0.43,"mean":0.5387500000000001,"n":64,"obs":0.234375,"sig":true},{"hi":0.81,"lo":0.65,"mean":0.7286567164179103,"n":67,"obs":0.40298507462686567,"sig":true},{"hi":0.92,"lo":0.81,"mean":0.8616949152542374,"n":59,"obs":0.4915254237288136,"sig":true},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.92,"mean":0.9867156862745099,"n":204,"obs":0.7647058823529411,"sig":true}],"prcp_km":8.9,"provisional":false,"rank":159,"rank_hi":180.0,"rank_lo":94.0,"reliability":0.04960796789733049,"resolution":0.09043265335593971,"skill_pct":null,"slug":"haiphong","station":"","timezone":"Asia/Bangkok"}